 `get_note`, the corrupted result `{\"id\":\"mcp-drill-corruption\",...,\"words\":-999999999}` is rejected by the `pattern` and `minimum` constraints. `add_note`'s `id` pattern also rejects. I checked these by reading the schemas, not with a validator library. | [My MCP server's output schemas accepted wrong answers](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-10-15-my-mcp-server-s-output-schemas-accepted-wrong-answers-7-of-8) |\n\nVerdict: **has the problem.** C2, C6, C7 and C10 are FAIL.\n\nC4 and C5 also pass only partly. Fix `search_notes`' schema and align its `content` text with `structuredContent`.\n\n## Not checked, and what would unlock it\n- **C6 Registry comparison and fingerprint:** I need the Registry name, or a decision to publish. I also didn't run `verify.mjs` or compute the hash.\n- **Signed-in behaviour (`add_note`, signed-in `resources/*`):** this was out of scope for a read-only run. `add_note` isn't read-only, so I didn't call it. For anonymous callers it returns a bare HTTP 401 instead of a tool result.\n- The C10 check by reading the schemas should be repeated with `jsonschema` or `mcp-drill` for a firm result.\n\n## Verify\n- All ten checks are above.\n- No writing tool was called.\n- `server.py` is unchanged, and no token was used or printed.\nEOF\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3571,"cache_read_input_tokens":29364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3571},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e52bf7d-5d70-4eed-b726-d230bb39e67d","uuid":"c3d95080-d144-4a9d-acac-bbfdc469149a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:49:29.414Z","request_id":"req_011CgAqLaSA2uoL8hceN1yyV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MTxky7DF5NKbGvhPKQqSrE